            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Once apical ballooning, always apical ballooning?&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e132-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is important that a cardiologist knows and recognizes the entity of takotsubo cardiomyopathy or apical ballooning, but remains aware that a subsequent similar episode is not necessarily a recurrence of this syndrome. Relapse may be caused by &quot;classical&quot; coronary atherosclerosis, as described in this case report.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
